        "geology": "Two geological formations are found. The East edge of the area belongs to the Iullemmeden sedimentary basin, Continental-Terminal : Mio-pliocene period Pre-cambrian gneisses, schists and granites. The western edge is part of the plutonic Liptako Gourma massif. The latter is part of the West African craton and consists of extensively weathered pre-cambrian. The boundary between the two formations roughly follows the River Niger.",
        "hydrology": "Endorheic surface hydrology with small-scale catchments converging to temporary ponds, with no presently active large-scale hydrographic network.\r\n",
        "soils": "Soils are essentially of the tropical ferrallitic type, sandy and weakly structured.",
        "vegetation": "The vegetation cover consists of a patchwork of three distinct basic units : tiger bush on the plateaus, fallow savanna and pearl millet fields on the sandy slopes."
      },
